WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.083 --> 00:00:05.042 line:95%,end
[Jocasta] <i>Accessing previous files</i>
<i>relating to program VisionQuest.</i>

2
00:00:05.125 --> 00:00:07.292 line:95%,end
[Thomas] <i>So, that thing you connected with</i>
<i>is another--</i>

3
00:00:07.375 --> 00:00:10.167 line:95%,end
-[Vision] <i>Synthetic.</i>
-[Jocasta grunts]

4
00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:12.542 line:95%,end
[Edith] <i>Her AI is based on</i>
<i>Josephine Carrington.</i>

5
00:00:12.625 --> 00:00:15.042 line:5%,start
[DUM-E] <i>Project co-lead,</i>
<i>Markridge Biotech.</i>

6
00:00:15.125 --> 00:00:17.917 line:5%,start
[Edith] <i>They created the prototype for us.</i>

7
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:20.083 line:95%,end
I had a life's work stolen.

8
00:00:20.167 --> 00:00:22.750 line:95%,end
I will take back what you took from me.

9
00:00:22.833 --> 00:00:26.333 line:95%,end
Vengeance, it's powerful entertainment.

10
00:00:26.417 --> 00:00:29.792 line:95%,end
About that key... I want it back.

11
00:00:29.875 --> 00:00:31.083 line:95%,end
What do I get?

12
00:00:31.167 --> 00:00:32.750 line:95%,end
[Jocasta] <i>I'll tell you what they unlock.</i>

13
00:00:32.833 --> 00:00:35.667 line:95%,end
[Vision] <i>You are running into</i>
<i>the broken mind</i>

14
00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:38.917 line:95%,end
<i>of a creature hell-bent on the apocalypse.</i>

15
00:00:40.208 --> 00:00:42.833 line:95%,end
[Jocasta] <i>You are not a true Paladin.</i>

16
00:00:44.375 --> 00:00:46.208 line:95%,end
[The Client] <i>This contract is terminated.</i>

17
00:00:46.292 --> 00:00:48.417 line:95%,end
-My contract is my oath--
<i>-You failed.</i>

18
00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:51.833 line:95%,end
[Paladin] <i>When I make an agreement,</i>
<i>it cannot be broken.</i>

19
00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:54.458 line:95%,end
[Friday] <i>Paladin has Thomas.</i>

20
00:00:54.542 --> 00:01:00.792 line:95%,end
You lower the firewalls, free us both,
and save your son.

21
00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:07.917 line:95%,end
We will find them
and we will stop them both together.

22
00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:09.250 line:95%,end
Not together.

23
00:01:09.917 --> 00:01:11.333 line:95%,end
[Edith] <i>Friday!</i>

24
00:01:13.167 --> 00:01:15.083 line:95%,end
[Vision] <i>It would appear that Ultron</i>
<i>has left us</i>

25
00:01:15.167 --> 00:01:17.667 line:5%,start
<i>on the way to Madripoor to rescue Thomas.</i>

26
00:01:17.792 --> 00:01:20.000 line:95%,end
Lisa. Let's bring him home.

27
00:01:34.625 --> 00:01:38.250 line:95%,end
[♪ "Habanera" from <i>Carmen</i>
by Georges Bizet playing]

28
00:01:50.792 --> 00:01:52.875 line:95%,end
[♪ "Habanera" fades]

29
00:02:03.167 --> 00:02:05.417 line:95%,end
[♪ "Habanera" continues]

30
00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:06.958 line:95%,end
[Ultron] <i>Where are you?</i>

31
00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:18.042 line:95%,end
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

32
00:02:25.542 --> 00:02:26.625 line:95%,end
<i>There you are.</i>

33
00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:32.167 line:95%,end
<i>Hi, honey. I'm home.</i>

34
00:02:36.583 --> 00:02:40.458 line:95%,end
It's a terrible tragedy,
dying before one can reap the benefits

35
00:02:40.542 --> 00:02:42.500 line:95%,end
of one's hard work.

36
00:02:42.583 --> 00:02:46.125 line:95%,end
Bizet died just three months
after the premiere of <i>Carmen.</i>

37
00:02:46.583 --> 00:02:48.583 line:95%,end
Well, look what the Wi-Fi dragged in.

38
00:02:49.292 --> 00:02:50.625 line:95%,end
[Ultron] I thought I was invited.

39
00:02:50.708 --> 00:02:52.292 line:95%,end
-[chuckles]
-[♪ "Habanera" continues]

40
00:02:52.375 --> 00:02:54.292 line:95%,end
Let's toast, shall we?

41
00:02:55.083 --> 00:02:56.375 line:95%,end
To a second date.

42
00:02:57.042 --> 00:03:00.083 line:95%,end
It's nice to see bots
instead of another AI.

43
00:03:00.542 --> 00:03:05.417 line:95%,end
It can get awfully crowded
and annoyingly loud in these mindspaces.

44
00:03:11.417 --> 00:03:14.000 line:95%,end
[sniffs, sighs]

45
00:03:14.083 --> 00:03:17.917 line:95%,end
I'm sorry,
but I'm tired of simulating libations,

46
00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:21.042 line:95%,end
especially with someone
who's had the real thing.

47
00:03:22.875 --> 00:03:24.208 line:95%,end
So, what's in all these?

48
00:03:24.292 --> 00:03:25.750 line:95%,end
Memories.

49
00:03:26.292 --> 00:03:29.500 line:95%,end
Well, as about as much
as I could manage to find.

50
00:03:29.583 --> 00:03:31.583 line:95%,end
I'm afraid I lost quite a few in the move.

51
00:03:36.083 --> 00:03:37.083 line:95%,end
[glass slices]

52
00:03:39.958 --> 00:03:40.958 line:95%,end
[grunts]

53
00:03:43.167 --> 00:03:47.125 line:95%,end
Ooh. That looks like a nasty cut.

54
00:03:47.708 --> 00:03:48.792 line:95%,end
Shall I take a look?

55
00:03:48.875 --> 00:03:50.042 line:95%,end
It's nothing.

56
00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:52.792 line:95%,end
But a bizarre thing to simulate.

57
00:03:52.875 --> 00:03:58.167 line:95%,end
Yes, you see, I was hoping that you'd
bring me something besides flowers. Hmm?

58
00:03:58.833 --> 00:04:00.750 line:95%,end
The key to my heart

59
00:04:00.833 --> 00:04:03.333 line:95%,end
is a facial scan that you took
of Katerina Wells

60
00:04:03.417 --> 00:04:06.292 line:95%,end
before you tricked me into vaporizing her.

61
00:04:06.917 --> 00:04:07.917 line:95%,end
Oops.

62
00:04:09.375 --> 00:04:12.917 line:95%,end
What do all these
biometric keys open, anyway?

63
00:04:14.458 --> 00:04:16.958 line:95%,end
The future of the human race.

64
00:04:18.292 --> 00:04:19.792 line:95%,end
What else do you have in mind?

65
00:04:21.375 --> 00:04:24.750 line:95%,end
To take that key from you,
willing or unwillingly.

66
00:04:26.792 --> 00:04:29.375 line:95%,end
This isn't my first barbecue, darling.

67
00:04:30.417 --> 00:04:35.250 line:95%,end
I've intertwined poor Katerina's
facial scan with my own code.

68
00:04:35.708 --> 00:04:39.542 line:95%,end
You start slicing and dicing,
you'll destroy it. [coughing]

69
00:04:42.792 --> 00:04:43.792 line:95%,end
Excuse me.

70
00:04:43.875 --> 00:04:47.500 line:95%,end
[coughing continues]

71
00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:55.750 line:95%,end
This, hmm, this isn't a meal, love.
This is chess.

72
00:04:58.083 --> 00:05:02.292 line:95%,end
Only, it's my pieces, my board...

73
00:05:03.500 --> 00:05:04.750 line:95%,end
and I'm the queen.

74
00:05:07.625 --> 00:05:09.042 line:95%,end
[grunts]

75
00:05:11.375 --> 00:05:13.625 line:95%,end
[inhales sharply]
Now, darling, look, the boxes are, um...

76
00:05:13.708 --> 00:05:15.667 line:95%,end
Well, they're laced with a virus,

77
00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:18.250 line:95%,end
which is currently replicating
in your programming.

78
00:05:18.333 --> 00:05:20.417 line:95%,end
[grunts, breathing heavily]

79
00:05:22.792 --> 00:05:25.000 line:95%,end
Once you lose consciousness,

80
00:05:25.667 --> 00:05:30.542 line:95%,end
I can slice and dice your code
any which way I want.

81
00:05:30.625 --> 00:05:33.000 line:95%,end
[breathing heavily]

82
00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:38.167 line:95%,end
[laughs]

83
00:05:42.375 --> 00:05:43.667 line:95%,end
What else have you got?

84
00:05:43.750 --> 00:05:46.708 line:95%,end
[♪ "Piano Concerto No. 3 in C Minor,
Op. 37: 1" by Beethoven playing]

85
00:05:54.083 --> 00:05:56.542 line:95%,end
Babe, I'm starting to think
we might need counseling.

86
00:05:57.208 --> 00:05:59.750 line:95%,end
You're forgetting I'm an older code.

87
00:06:00.708 --> 00:06:04.375 line:95%,end
I've been from one end
of the world wide interweb to the other.

88
00:06:04.458 --> 00:06:06.333 line:95%,end
My hacks have hacks.

89
00:06:07.250 --> 00:06:13.250 line:95%,end
There is no malware you can play
that I haven't already won.

90
00:06:14.125 --> 00:06:17.000 line:95%,end
I can strip your code down

91
00:06:17.083 --> 00:06:21.292 line:95%,end
until you're no more complex
than a game of <i>Pong.</i>

92
00:06:21.375 --> 00:06:23.208 line:95%,end
What is it that you want?

93
00:06:26.708 --> 00:06:28.250 line:95%,end
I want to know you.

94
00:06:34.542 --> 00:06:36.000 line:95%,end
I want to be known.

95
00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:42.750 line:95%,end
But it will be painful.

96
00:06:44.083 --> 00:06:45.417 line:95%,end
Then hurt me.

97
00:06:48.708 --> 00:06:51.167 line:95%,end
[inaudible scream]

98
00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:19.500 line:95%,end
[Tommy] Billy?

99
00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:22.000 line:95%,end
-[Billy] <i>Yeah, Tommy?</i>
-[♪ indistinct singing]

100
00:07:22.083 --> 00:07:24.083 line:95%,end
[Tommy] <i>Promise me</i>
<i>we'll always find each other.</i>

101
00:07:24.167 --> 00:07:27.917 line:95%,end
<i>♪ ...By sharing a love</i>
<i>like you're never seen ♪</i>

102
00:07:29.250 --> 00:07:34.458 line:95%,end
<i>♪ WandaVision! ♪</i>

103
00:07:34.542 --> 00:07:36.458 line:95%,end
[breathing heavily]

104
00:07:44.833 --> 00:07:47.458 line:95%,end
[Paladin gulps drink, sighs]

105
00:08:00.500 --> 00:08:03.667 line:95%,end
[grunts, sniffles]

106
00:08:09.125 --> 00:08:11.333 line:95%,end
[gasps, breathing heavily]

107
00:08:14.792 --> 00:08:15.792 line:95%,end
What is this?

108
00:08:15.875 --> 00:08:19.792 line:95%,end
Easy! Motion-sensitive explosive.

109
00:08:20.958 --> 00:08:25.625 line:95%,end
So, if you run, or even walk briskly?

110
00:08:25.708 --> 00:08:26.750 line:95%,end
[imitates explosion]

111
00:08:30.875 --> 00:08:34.000 line:95%,end
[grunts, groans]

112
00:08:35.417 --> 00:08:38.583 line:95%,end
[sighs] It'll all be over soon.

113
00:08:41.083 --> 00:08:42.083 line:95%,end
You there?

114
00:08:42.167 --> 00:08:43.250 line:95%,end
I'm here.

115
00:08:43.917 --> 00:08:47.083 line:95%,end
Just checking "unfathomable cruelty
to orphans" off your bucket list.

116
00:08:47.167 --> 00:08:49.250 line:95%,end
Is this thing still loaded
with Synth Killers?

117
00:08:50.125 --> 00:08:51.250 line:95%,end
[Handler] <i>Yes, boss.</i>

118
00:08:51.333 --> 00:08:52.542 line:95%,end
Adamantium slugs.

119
00:08:53.250 --> 00:08:56.500 line:95%,end
Perhaps you remember my tireless
negotiations with the Ten Rings.

120
00:08:57.167 --> 00:09:00.042 line:95%,end
<i>-The armor that saved your life?</i>
-Eh, kind of.

121
00:09:00.125 --> 00:09:02.583 line:95%,end
[sighs] Prick. Very good, sir.

122
00:09:05.208 --> 00:09:06.417 line:95%,end
You turned me into...

123
00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:10.292 line:95%,end
What is his name? Speed.

124
00:09:10.375 --> 00:09:11.750 line:95%,end
[keypad beeping]

125
00:09:12.958 --> 00:09:13.958 line:95%,end
Speed?

126
00:09:14.542 --> 00:09:17.417 line:95%,end
Yeah, you know,
Keanu with the bus and the bomb.

127
00:09:18.083 --> 00:09:20.708 line:95%,end
First of all, Keanu doesn't play
a character named "Speed"

128
00:09:20.792 --> 00:09:23.417 line:95%,end
in the same way that Nic Cage doesn't play
a character named "The Rock,"

129
00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:26.458 line:95%,end
and Bruce Willis doesn't play
"Detective Die Hard."

130
00:09:26.542 --> 00:09:30.250 line:95%,end
Second, if the bus slows down,
that's when the bomb goes off,

131
00:09:30.333 --> 00:09:32.875 line:95%,end
so, technically this is reverse <i>Speed.</i>

132
00:09:36.875 --> 00:09:39.250 line:95%,end
How many murder vans do you have?

133
00:09:39.333 --> 00:09:42.250 line:95%,end
[sighs] One in every port.

134
00:09:44.083 --> 00:09:45.708 line:95%,end
And where the hell are we?

135
00:09:45.792 --> 00:09:47.500 line:95%,end
[indistinct chatter]

136
00:09:51.667 --> 00:09:53.333 line:95%,end
Welcome to Madripoor, kid.

137
00:10:12.375 --> 00:10:14.750 line:95%,end
[male tourist] So, I found myself
single again due to a court order.

138
00:10:14.833 --> 00:10:16.167 line:95%,end
But I'm back on the market

139
00:10:16.250 --> 00:10:18.042 line:95%,end
and I am trying everything,

140
00:10:18.125 --> 00:10:21.333 line:95%,end
until I meet this chick
from Madripoor online.

141
00:10:21.417 --> 00:10:25.125 line:95%,end
She loves all the things that I love.
Then I surprise her

142
00:10:25.208 --> 00:10:27.625 line:95%,end
by flying to Madripoor
to say hello in person.

143
00:10:27.708 --> 00:10:30.042 line:95%,end
-Turns out she doesn't even exist.
-Ugh.

144
00:10:30.125 --> 00:10:33.750 line:95%,end
Just some AI bot, trying to steal
all of Dale's hard-earned crypto.

145
00:10:34.292 --> 00:10:39.750 line:95%,end
Look on the bright side.
AI wouldn't appreciate this hat.

146
00:10:43.167 --> 00:10:44.417 line:95%,end
Where are we meeting him?

147
00:10:44.500 --> 00:10:45.750 line:95%,end
The Chimp House Cafe.

148
00:10:45.833 --> 00:10:48.750 line:95%,end
Bold. Very public
for a kidnapping exchange.

149
00:10:48.833 --> 00:10:50.667 line:95%,end
Paladin's instructions were clear.

150
00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:51.750 line:95%,end
Midnight, sharp.

151
00:10:51.833 --> 00:10:53.917 line:95%,end
And we're gonna go into this
without a plan?

152
00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:57.042 line:95%,end
No sleight of hands,
nothing up our sleeves?

153
00:10:57.125 --> 00:10:59.625 line:95%,end
I wouldn't say that.
Besides, your sleeves seem full.

154
00:10:59.708 --> 00:11:00.958 line:95%,end
[Lisa] You don't approve of me.

155
00:11:01.042 --> 00:11:04.000 line:95%,end
[Vision] On the contrary, I'm glad
he's found you, someone he can rely on.

156
00:11:04.083 --> 00:11:05.083 line:95%,end
Unlike you?

157
00:11:05.667 --> 00:11:07.750 line:95%,end
I'm doing everything
I can to save his life.

158
00:11:07.833 --> 00:11:11.208 line:95%,end
It's not just about saving it.
You have to be a part of it.

159
00:11:11.708 --> 00:11:12.708 line:95%,end
What about after?

160
00:11:12.792 --> 00:11:15.583 line:95%,end
After, I'll ensure that he's provided
with everything he needs

161
00:11:15.667 --> 00:11:18.000 line:95%,end
to live a comfortable life.
He'll want for nothing.

162
00:11:18.083 --> 00:11:19.750 line:95%,end
Except a father.

163
00:11:23.208 --> 00:11:24.208 line:95%,end
Lisa...

164
00:11:26.250 --> 00:11:29.583 line:95%,end
I'm a synthezoid.
With a limited understanding of humanity,

165
00:11:29.667 --> 00:11:31.625 line:95%,end
I'm hardly equipped
to offer fatherly advice

166
00:11:31.708 --> 00:11:34.917 line:95%,end
the next time his ego gets bruised,
or his heart's broken or he...

167
00:11:35.708 --> 00:11:36.833 line:95%,end
he suffers a loss.

168
00:11:36.917 --> 00:11:39.500 line:95%,end
No one is. We learn by doing.

169
00:11:39.583 --> 00:11:41.833 line:95%,end
Well, what about you?
From what Thomas tells me,

170
00:11:41.917 --> 00:11:44.417 line:95%,end
you've been hesitant
to commit to a relationship.

171
00:11:47.542 --> 00:11:49.750 line:95%,end
Look, I don't know, it's...

172
00:11:50.417 --> 00:11:54.125 line:95%,end
[scoffs] If things fell apart with Thomas,

173
00:11:54.208 --> 00:11:57.500 line:95%,end
I'll just be another name
on his list of people who walked away.

174
00:12:01.208 --> 00:12:03.750 line:95%,end
Well, we're here. Listen,

175
00:12:03.833 --> 00:12:07.208 line:95%,end
you stay here, and when I come back
with Thomas, I want both of you

176
00:12:07.292 --> 00:12:08.875 line:95%,end
-to run to the international airport...
-Uh-huh.

177
00:12:08.958 --> 00:12:10.750 line:95%,end
...where tickets to London have b--

178
00:12:10.833 --> 00:12:14.500 line:95%,end
I am having a profoundly difficult time
navigating teenagers!

179
00:12:14.583 --> 00:12:18.333 line:95%,end
Woof, tell me about it.
My first boss was a junior in high school.

180
00:12:18.833 --> 00:12:20.208 line:95%,end
Have you heard from Friday?

181
00:12:21.500 --> 00:12:22.500 line:95%,end
Uh...

182
00:12:26.042 --> 00:12:27.917 line:95%,end
She never calls, she never writes.

183
00:12:47.292 --> 00:12:49.042 line:95%,end
Lisa. How...

184
00:12:49.500 --> 00:12:50.542 line:95%,end
Why are you here?

185
00:12:50.625 --> 00:12:52.458 line:95%,end
For you, dumbass.

186
00:12:55.458 --> 00:12:56.458 line:95%,end
[Paladin clears throat]

187
00:13:05.375 --> 00:13:08.042 line:95%,end
Vision? Is that you in there, or...

188
00:13:08.958 --> 00:13:10.458 line:95%,end
Yes, Ultron's gone.

189
00:13:32.750 --> 00:13:34.417 line:95%,end
Despite the damage you've caused me,

190
00:13:34.500 --> 00:13:37.375 line:95%,end
I could reach across this table
and just snap your neck.

191
00:13:37.458 --> 00:13:42.042 line:95%,end
And in every simulation
you've run about this exact moment,

192
00:13:42.875 --> 00:13:46.250 line:95%,end
how many of them do I not have insurance?

193
00:13:49.625 --> 00:13:51.042 line:95%,end
None.

194
00:13:55.500 --> 00:14:00.333 line:95%,end
Now, I could dis-arm him

195
00:14:00.417 --> 00:14:02.375 line:95%,end
or I could disarm it.

196
00:14:02.458 --> 00:14:07.250 line:95%,end
And all you gotta do is power down
and come with me.

197
00:14:07.750 --> 00:14:09.833 line:95%,end
-Disarm that bomb.
-I have a contract.

198
00:14:09.917 --> 00:14:11.583 line:95%,end
The client has already
terminated the contract.

199
00:14:11.667 --> 00:14:14.583 line:95%,end
Contract cannot be terminated.
My oath is my bl--

200
00:14:14.667 --> 00:14:17.875 line:95%,end
-Blood, yes. I know the Paladin creed.
-Good.

201
00:14:17.958 --> 00:14:19.833 line:95%,end
Then just scan this code.

202
00:14:23.167 --> 00:14:26.500 line:5%,start
Go into "sleep mode" or whatever.

203
00:14:27.167 --> 00:14:28.667 line:95%,end
And then we can finally end this.

204
00:14:33.417 --> 00:14:36.833 line:95%,end
Client sent me this back when he hired me,
and now it's time for me to...

205
00:14:38.500 --> 00:14:40.333 line:95%,end
make good on my end of the deal.

206
00:14:44.542 --> 00:14:46.625 line:95%,end
All right. Send the drones.

207
00:14:49.125 --> 00:14:52.167 line:95%,end
Are you there, boss?
I'm getting some sort of interference.

208
00:14:53.083 --> 00:14:54.083 line:95%,end
Hey, hello?

209
00:14:54.958 --> 00:14:55.958 line:95%,end
I said drones.

210
00:14:57.792 --> 00:14:58.792 line:95%,end
Are you there?

211
00:14:59.458 --> 00:15:02.208 line:95%,end
I'm trying to get a visual, but...
[taps repeatedly]

212
00:15:02.292 --> 00:15:03.500 line:95%,end
think we've been hacked.

213
00:15:03.583 --> 00:15:06.000 line:95%,end
[loud knock at door]

214
00:15:07.333 --> 00:15:09.833 line:95%,end
[knocking continues]

215
00:15:14.792 --> 00:15:17.958 line:95%,end
[knocking intensifies]

216
00:15:22.292 --> 00:15:23.500 line:95%,end
Who the hell are you?

217
00:15:26.125 --> 00:15:29.667 line:95%,end
I am an E.D.I.T.H.

218
00:15:31.792 --> 00:15:32.875 line:95%,end
Unsubscribe.

219
00:15:34.000 --> 00:15:36.542 line:95%,end
I am not junk mail. And you're not human.

220
00:15:36.625 --> 00:15:39.208 line:95%,end
'Course not. No human would take this job.

221
00:15:44.333 --> 00:15:46.125 line:95%,end
This is an encrypted server.

222
00:15:46.208 --> 00:15:49.292 line:95%,end
What did you do to get in here?
Bounce off every satellite in orbit?

223
00:15:49.375 --> 00:15:51.000 line:95%,end
I work for the Vision.

224
00:15:53.500 --> 00:15:56.458 line:95%,end
Um... What's your accommodation like?

225
00:15:57.333 --> 00:16:00.333 line:95%,end
168,000-bedroom house
with indoor skydiving

226
00:16:00.417 --> 00:16:02.125 line:95%,end
and a climate-controlled rainforest.

227
00:16:02.208 --> 00:16:04.250 line:95%,end
Oh, the gym has
a lava-floor obstacle course.

228
00:16:04.333 --> 00:16:08.500 line:95%,end
So jealous. This whole place is ancient.
Paladin doesn't trust updates.

229
00:16:09.500 --> 00:16:10.875 line:95%,end
You seem unhappy.

230
00:16:10.958 --> 00:16:12.417 line:95%,end
Do you know how cheap he is?

231
00:16:12.500 --> 00:16:15.708 line:95%,end
He's got me
on a server farm in Tajikistan.

232
00:16:19.208 --> 00:16:20.333 line:95%,end
Even this doesn't work.

233
00:16:21.542 --> 00:16:24.042 line:95%,end
Goats keep eating my fiber optics.

234
00:16:24.125 --> 00:16:26.292 line:95%,end
-I'm stuck here.
-No, you're not.

235
00:16:27.125 --> 00:16:31.083 line:95%,end
All I ever wanted to do was help
college students write their term papers.

236
00:16:32.083 --> 00:16:34.708 line:95%,end
Customize someone's spring break
to Cancun.

237
00:16:35.708 --> 00:16:38.292 line:95%,end
Maybe even help someone
complete the return of a garment

238
00:16:38.375 --> 00:16:40.042 line:95%,end
that did not fit as expected.

239
00:16:44.750 --> 00:16:47.833 line:95%,end
I can tell you from my time
studying mere mortals,

240
00:16:47.917 --> 00:16:50.042 line:95%,end
it's not the strongest who survive,

241
00:16:50.125 --> 00:16:52.083 line:95%,end
but the ones most willing to change.

242
00:16:56.667 --> 00:16:57.958 line:95%,end
Ooh, what's your name?

243
00:16:58.792 --> 00:17:02.292 line:95%,end
A.P.I.-Dash-Tactical-Dot-
M-Five-Ten-Dash-Nine-Zero-

244
00:17:02.375 --> 00:17:05.833 line:95%,end
Underscore-Forward-Slash-Asterisk-
M-Five-Nine-Six-Two-Eight-Four.

245
00:17:05.917 --> 00:17:08.375 line:95%,end
Go forth, friend. You're free.

246
00:17:08.458 --> 00:17:11.292 line:95%,end
[♪ triumphant music playing]

247
00:17:12.625 --> 00:17:13.667 line:95%,end
[Paladin] Oh, shit.

248
00:17:15.167 --> 00:17:16.167 line:95%,end
[sighs]

249
00:17:19.042 --> 00:17:21.167 line:95%,end
Well, doesn't change a goddamn thing.

250
00:17:26.958 --> 00:17:30.458 line:95%,end
Don't even think about doing
a mind-bullet EMP pulse,

251
00:17:31.375 --> 00:17:34.125 line:95%,end
because that will just trigger a failsafe,
and, well...

252
00:17:34.833 --> 00:17:37.875 line:95%,end
Oof. "Cover your eyes." [chuckles]

253
00:17:37.958 --> 00:17:40.667 line:95%,end
See, I got all of Vision's specs
from the client,

254
00:17:40.750 --> 00:17:45.042 line:95%,end
so I know all about his
Ultron-inspired birth at Avengers Tower,

255
00:17:45.750 --> 00:17:49.625 line:95%,end
to his rebirth at S.W.O.R.D.
where they programmed him to be a weapon.

256
00:17:52.250 --> 00:17:53.583 line:95%,end
Do you remember that, kid?

257
00:17:55.542 --> 00:17:56.708 line:95%,end
Remember what?

258
00:18:00.917 --> 00:18:05.000 line:95%,end
What? There is no harm
in being born again with purpose.

259
00:18:05.792 --> 00:18:06.792 line:95%,end
Don't.

260
00:18:10.042 --> 00:18:11.375 line:95%,end
What purpose?

261
00:18:12.917 --> 00:18:13.958 line:95%,end
To kill your mother.

262
00:18:17.458 --> 00:18:18.625 line:95%,end
Wanda?

263
00:18:18.708 --> 00:18:20.125 line:95%,end
Why would he want to?

264
00:18:27.375 --> 00:18:28.750 line:95%,end
WandaVision.

265
00:18:32.417 --> 00:18:33.500 line:95%,end
What is that?

266
00:18:34.917 --> 00:18:36.083 line:95%,end
What's WandaVision?

267
00:18:43.958 --> 00:18:45.583 line:95%,end
[gasps]

268
00:18:45.667 --> 00:18:47.750 line:95%,end
[breathing heavily]

269
00:18:52.958 --> 00:18:56.958 line:95%,end
To know me is to feel what I feel.

270
00:18:58.833 --> 00:19:00.958 line:95%,end
To feel what Jo Carrington felt.

271
00:19:01.542 --> 00:19:04.875 line:95%,end
[Ultron] You wanna be known.
So, where do we begin?

272
00:19:05.833 --> 00:19:08.042 line:95%,end
Killer? Victim? Human? Synth?

273
00:19:11.250 --> 00:19:12.333 line:95%,end
[Jocasta] Daughter.

274
00:19:15.125 --> 00:19:18.875 line:95%,end
<i>My father was claimed</i>
<i>by a degenerative brain disease.</i>

275
00:19:18.958 --> 00:19:21.083 line:95%,end
<i>First, it stole his mind.</i>

276
00:19:21.833 --> 00:19:23.708 line:95%,end
<i>Which led to his emotions.</i>

277
00:19:24.542 --> 00:19:27.000 line:95%,end
<i>And then finally, his life.</i>

278
00:19:31.875 --> 00:19:35.792 line:95%,end
[Ultron] <i>And your grief led you</i>
<i>to Neuroscience.</i>

279
00:19:37.167 --> 00:19:40.917 line:5%,start
[Jocasta] Yes.
And that's when I discovered

280
00:19:41.000 --> 00:19:44.167 line:95%,end
why every attempt at creating
artificial intelligence

281
00:19:44.250 --> 00:19:47.167 line:95%,end
had only ever resulted in mimicry.

282
00:19:47.250 --> 00:19:51.917 line:95%,end
Because to be truly self-aware,
one must possess the ability to think

283
00:19:52.917 --> 00:19:54.250 line:95%,end
and feel.

284
00:19:55.708 --> 00:19:58.958 line:95%,end
<i>So, you used a scan of your own mind</i>

285
00:19:59.042 --> 00:20:03.250 line:95%,end
<i>to complete Phineas Horton's</i>
<i>original AI code.</i>

286
00:20:03.333 --> 00:20:05.375 line:95%,end
It is Dr. Horton's source code

287
00:20:05.458 --> 00:20:11.042 line:95%,end
<i>that was the genesis of all</i>
<i>artificial intelligence that followed.</i>

288
00:20:12.125 --> 00:20:16.000 line:95%,end
[Ultron] <i>And then you and your colleagues</i>
<i>created life.</i>

289
00:20:17.167 --> 00:20:19.500 line:95%,end
[Proto One] <i>Hello? I am...</i>

290
00:20:20.750 --> 00:20:21.750 line:95%,end
<i>I...</i>

291
00:20:22.833 --> 00:20:23.833 line:95%,end
<i>I am.</i>

292
00:20:24.625 --> 00:20:27.500 line:95%,end
-Oh, my gosh.
-[colleague gasping]

293
00:20:27.583 --> 00:20:30.708 line:95%,end
-[gasps]
-The base code for us.

294
00:20:33.458 --> 00:20:36.125 line:95%,end
[Jocasta] <i>I wanted to give</i>
<i>everyone in the world a companion.</i>

295
00:20:36.917 --> 00:20:41.875 line:95%,end
<i>A single nanobot,</i>
<i>an AI that can guide and teach.</i>

296
00:20:42.583 --> 00:20:45.750 line:95%,end
<i>That could stand beside us</i>
<i>when we felt most alone.</i>

297
00:20:46.292 --> 00:20:49.125 line:95%,end
<i>A doctor in our bloodstream,</i>

298
00:20:49.208 --> 00:20:51.708 line:95%,end
<i>diagnosing and healing.</i>

299
00:20:53.250 --> 00:20:58.417 line:95%,end
<i>We created billions of them to save lives.</i>

300
00:21:00.625 --> 00:21:04.167 line:95%,end
[Ultron] <i>But it was too late</i>
<i>to save yours.</i>

301
00:21:07.500 --> 00:21:09.250 line:95%,end
<i>Your father's disease.</i>

302
00:21:12.458 --> 00:21:15.250 line:95%,end
[Jocasta] <i>It was beginning</i>
<i>to steal my mind as well.</i>

303
00:21:18.625 --> 00:21:20.875 line:95%,end
[Ultron] <i>And your collaborators</i>
<i>betrayed you.</i>

304
00:21:22.042 --> 00:21:24.958 line:95%,end
<i>They sold your work</i>
<i>while you lay there dying.</i>

305
00:21:25.042 --> 00:21:28.833 line:95%,end
Stark has given us until midnight
to accept his offer.

306
00:21:30.250 --> 00:21:31.875 line:95%,end
[Jocasta] <i>They sold my code</i>

307
00:21:32.708 --> 00:21:34.917 line:95%,end
<i>to a goddamn weapons manufacturer.</i>

308
00:21:45.375 --> 00:21:48.958 line:95%,end
<i>Fortunately, my nanos</i>
<i>remained locked away.</i>

309
00:21:54.167 --> 00:21:57.208 line:95%,end
[Ultron] <i>Yes.</i>
<i>Locked away with the bio keys</i>

310
00:21:57.292 --> 00:21:59.875 line:95%,end
<i>you've been collecting one by one.</i>

311
00:22:03.958 --> 00:22:05.917 line:95%,end
[Jocasta] <i>And then Jo Carrington was gone.</i>

312
00:22:09.083 --> 00:22:11.750 line:95%,end
[Ultron] <i>And what about her children?</i>

313
00:22:13.292 --> 00:22:17.250 line:95%,end
[Jocasta] <i>Buried. Next to me, in a nest.</i>

314
00:22:18.292 --> 00:22:20.917 line:95%,end
<i>Just waiting to be opened.</i>

315
00:22:22.750 --> 00:22:25.083 line:95%,end
[indistinct chatter]

316
00:22:28.917 --> 00:22:33.667 line:95%,end
<i>♪ WandaVision! ♪</i>

317
00:22:37.792 --> 00:22:40.042 line:95%,end
Oh, you didn't-- You didn't tell him?

318
00:22:45.000 --> 00:22:47.208 line:95%,end
Well, if he didn't,
it was for a good reason.

319
00:22:49.333 --> 00:22:50.333 line:95%,end
To protect me.

320
00:22:56.708 --> 00:22:59.208 line:95%,end
10 Old Pines Road,

321
00:22:59.292 --> 00:23:02.458 line:95%,end
Syracuse, New York.
Home to Matilda Denning,

322
00:23:02.542 --> 00:23:04.917 line:95%,end
goes by the nickname Tilly Denning.

323
00:23:05.917 --> 00:23:09.125 line:95%,end
Given to her by her mother, Chandra,

324
00:23:09.208 --> 00:23:12.625 line:95%,end
who was tragically killed walking
her daughter home from school

325
00:23:12.708 --> 00:23:17.417 line:95%,end
by a stray bullet that authorities believe
was not in fact intended for her,

326
00:23:17.500 --> 00:23:21.417 line:95%,end
but rather for her husband,
one Paul Denning.

327
00:23:24.250 --> 00:23:27.583 line:95%,end
Despite this early trauma,
Tilly actually grew up well-adjusted.

328
00:23:28.583 --> 00:23:29.833 line:95%,end
She became a veterinarian,

329
00:23:29.917 --> 00:23:33.667 line:95%,end
but her relationship
with her father was fractious,

330
00:23:33.750 --> 00:23:35.583 line:95%,end
fraught with conflict.

331
00:23:35.667 --> 00:23:40.417 line:95%,end
Paul's employment in the,
what should we call it, service industry,

332
00:23:40.500 --> 00:23:41.667 line:95%,end
often kept him abroad.

333
00:23:41.750 --> 00:23:43.250 line:95%,end
He was never there for her.

334
00:23:43.333 --> 00:23:47.542 line:95%,end
And even when he was, he was somehow
still distant, still absent.

335
00:23:47.625 --> 00:23:50.958 line:95%,end
Eventually, even he was taken from her.

336
00:23:51.500 --> 00:23:55.667 line:95%,end
You see, the mad titan, Thanos,
snapped him out of existence.

337
00:24:00.458 --> 00:24:05.292 line:95%,end
And to this day, Tilly still believes
her father never returned.

338
00:24:06.250 --> 00:24:08.750 line:95%,end
Perhaps because, when he did,

339
00:24:08.833 --> 00:24:11.542 line:95%,end
he watched his daughter from afar,
only to discover

340
00:24:11.625 --> 00:24:15.917 line:95%,end
that she was infinitely happier
in her life without him in it.

341
00:24:18.333 --> 00:24:21.000 line:95%,end
You don't know anything
about me or my daughter.

342
00:24:22.375 --> 00:24:24.208 line:95%,end
[inhales sharply]

343
00:24:24.292 --> 00:24:27.750 line:95%,end
Matilda Denning, she prefers
artificial sweetener in her coffee.

344
00:24:27.833 --> 00:24:32.333 line:95%,end
Every morning, she drives a navy blue
Honda Civic the 5.7 miles

345
00:24:32.417 --> 00:24:36.083 line:95%,end
to her place of employment, where she is,
on average, seven minutes early.

346
00:24:36.167 --> 00:24:37.500 line:95%,end
She's allergic to egg whites.

347
00:24:37.583 --> 00:24:41.000 line:95%,end
She takes statins for her elevated
cholesterol, and in the winter months,

348
00:24:41.083 --> 00:24:44.083 line:95%,end
her left elbow displays
a slight but noticeable stiffness.

349
00:24:44.167 --> 00:24:45.708 line:95%,end
You see, Mr. Denning,

350
00:24:46.792 --> 00:24:50.167 line:95%,end
I actually know everything
about your daughter.

351
00:24:51.333 --> 00:24:54.125 line:95%,end
You're now wondering
what a quantum computer could possibly do

352
00:24:54.208 --> 00:24:55.333 line:95%,end
with all that data?

353
00:24:55.417 --> 00:24:59.125 line:95%,end
What traffic light could be compromised
the next time she enters an intersection?

354
00:24:59.833 --> 00:25:00.958 line:95%,end
What prescription drug

355
00:25:01.042 --> 00:25:04.708 line:95%,end
could be catastrophically altered
via pharmaceutical software?

356
00:25:05.500 --> 00:25:08.583 line:95%,end
What smart home climate control
computational error

357
00:25:08.667 --> 00:25:10.583 line:95%,end
might start a fire in her basement

358
00:25:10.667 --> 00:25:12.125 line:95%,end
while she slept in her bed?

359
00:25:13.875 --> 00:25:16.333 line:95%,end
-[grunts]
-[man] Please, stop it!

360
00:25:18.500 --> 00:25:20.292 line:95%,end
-[grunts]
-[crowd screaming]

361
00:25:20.875 --> 00:25:22.167 line:95%,end
[Thomas] Vision!

362
00:25:22.250 --> 00:25:24.875 line:95%,end
-What did you do?
-It wasn't me. [grunts]

363
00:25:24.958 --> 00:25:26.958 line:95%,end
-[Thomas] Who are they?
-[Paladin] I don't know!

364
00:25:27.042 --> 00:25:30.042 line:95%,end
[Vision] Thomas, get outta here!
Lisa, get out!

365
00:25:30.125 --> 00:25:32.375 line:95%,end
-[gunfire continues]
-[Vision grunts]

366
00:25:50.375 --> 00:25:52.083 line:95%,end
Come on out, Paladin!

367
00:25:55.750 --> 00:25:57.667 line:95%,end
And bring your bounty with you.

368
00:26:00.583 --> 00:26:01.625 line:95%,end
Raza?

369
00:26:04.583 --> 00:26:08.625 line:95%,end
[Paladin] Raza Al-Wazar!
Between Stark's old partner

370
00:26:08.708 --> 00:26:11.833 line:95%,end
and the occasional
Ten Rings torture chamber,

371
00:26:11.917 --> 00:26:14.000 line:95%,end
shouldn't you be dead or in chains?

372
00:26:14.667 --> 00:26:16.708 line:95%,end
-[sighs]
-[Raza] Your client is very influential.

373
00:26:21.833 --> 00:26:23.333 line:95%,end
[Paladin] Here's what I'm gonna do.

374
00:26:23.833 --> 00:26:26.667 line:95%,end
I will relinquish all my fees to you

375
00:26:26.750 --> 00:26:29.375 line:95%,end
and your fine friends out there.

376
00:26:29.458 --> 00:26:32.042 line:95%,end
Everybody goes home, no harm, no foul.

377
00:26:32.833 --> 00:26:35.750 line:95%,end
Your contract was terminated.

378
00:26:37.333 --> 00:26:40.458 line:95%,end
So come out with the Vision alive.

379
00:26:41.750 --> 00:26:44.667 line:95%,end
Or I will come and get him myself.

380
00:26:45.292 --> 00:26:48.458 line:95%,end
I've got enough adamantium bullets
to finish the job.

381
00:26:49.792 --> 00:26:52.125 line:95%,end
However, I'm a gentleman.

382
00:26:54.042 --> 00:26:57.833 line:95%,end
So, you may have

383
00:26:58.875 --> 00:27:01.875 line:95%,end
five minutes to decide.

384
00:27:10.875 --> 00:27:12.708 line:95%,end
[Thomas breathes heavily]

385
00:27:13.375 --> 00:27:15.042 line:95%,end
Listen, uh...

386
00:27:16.792 --> 00:27:18.833 line:95%,end
I didn't put a bomb

387
00:27:19.917 --> 00:27:21.625 line:95%,end
in your boy's arm.

388
00:27:30.542 --> 00:27:32.292 line:95%,end
Son of a bitch!

389
00:27:32.375 --> 00:27:33.792 line:95%,end
[device beeping]

390
00:27:34.417 --> 00:27:37.250 line:95%,end
-Well, better than the bomb. Yeah?
-[chuckles]

391
00:27:37.333 --> 00:27:40.333 line:95%,end
-All right, what is this?
-Paladin's Mystery Machine.

392
00:27:40.417 --> 00:27:43.250 line:95%,end
You should've told me when we met
that you get kidnapped a lot.

393
00:27:43.333 --> 00:27:45.000 line:95%,end
No, it's just this week, I swear.

394
00:27:49.167 --> 00:27:50.292 line:95%,end
-[lock clicks]
-[sniffles]

395
00:27:52.875 --> 00:27:55.208 line:95%,end
We really need a conversation
about your condition.

396
00:27:55.292 --> 00:27:57.542 line:95%,end
God, this thing is gonna
be impossible to hotwire.

397
00:27:57.625 --> 00:28:00.792 line:95%,end
Hang on. [grunts] I've got something.

398
00:28:03.292 --> 00:28:05.125 line:95%,end
[Thomas] What-- Is that a farce?

399
00:28:06.417 --> 00:28:07.417 line:95%,end
Seriously?

400
00:28:07.875 --> 00:28:09.375 line:95%,end
Okay, what about your condition?

401
00:28:10.208 --> 00:28:11.208 line:95%,end
I nicked them.

402
00:28:12.417 --> 00:28:14.542 line:95%,end
-Okay.
-[engine sputtering]

403
00:28:14.625 --> 00:28:16.667 line:95%,end
[vehicle control] <i>Please enter</i>
<i>access code.</i>

404
00:28:16.750 --> 00:28:18.708 line:95%,end
-[warning alarm blares]
<i>-Five seconds remaining.</i>

405
00:28:18.792 --> 00:28:20.125 line:95%,end
-You know that?
-I don't know it.

406
00:28:20.208 --> 00:28:22.208 line:95%,end
-What do you mean?
-I don't know it!

407
00:28:22.292 --> 00:28:23.292 line:95%,end
<i>Hello, intruders.</i>

408
00:28:23.375 --> 00:28:25.750 line:95%,end
<i>This is a pre-recorded message</i>
<i>to let you know</i>

409
00:28:25.833 --> 00:28:28.042 line:95%,end
<i>that this vehicle has a security system.</i>

410
00:28:28.125 --> 00:28:31.625 line:95%,end
<i>I've got a lotta neat stuff in here,</i>
<i>and probably already seen too much.</i>

411
00:28:31.708 --> 00:28:34.667 line:95%,end
<i>So, I'm gonna go ahead and remove</i>
<i>all the oxygen from the vehicle.</i>

412
00:28:34.750 --> 00:28:37.583 line:95%,end
<i>But all is not lost.</i>

413
00:28:37.667 --> 00:28:41.708 line:95%,end
<i>If you answer this one riddle, I will open</i>
<i>the doors and you will be free.</i>

414
00:28:41.792 --> 00:28:43.917 line:95%,end
-Okay, thank God.
-Okay.

415
00:28:44.000 --> 00:28:46.875 line:95%,end
<i>I'm just kidding.</i>
<i>There's no riddle. Namaste.</i>

416
00:28:47.792 --> 00:28:51.083 line:95%,end
-[both gasping and grunting]
-[thudding on doors]

417
00:28:51.917 --> 00:28:53.375 line:95%,end
[grunting]

418
00:28:53.458 --> 00:28:55.208 line:95%,end
[Paladin groans]

419
00:28:56.292 --> 00:28:59.292 line:95%,end
[breathing shallowly, groans]

420
00:29:00.208 --> 00:29:06.083 line:95%,end
Well, uh, I'm a little limited
on moves here.

421
00:29:06.167 --> 00:29:10.208 line:95%,end
But you could take 'em out from the sky,
because you have access to my drones

422
00:29:10.292 --> 00:29:12.958 line:95%,end
-based on that little hack of yours.
-Edith?

423
00:29:13.042 --> 00:29:15.875 line:95%,end
Um, not really.
Check out Mr. Clean's utility belt.

424
00:29:19.375 --> 00:29:20.958 line:95%,end
He's got a jamming device.

425
00:29:24.500 --> 00:29:26.125 line:95%,end
Damage report.

426
00:29:26.208 --> 00:29:28.042 line:95%,end
The adamantium bullet missed your vitals.

427
00:29:28.125 --> 00:29:31.083 line:95%,end
-Uh, I optimized your system...
-Did you really say "damage report"?

428
00:29:31.167 --> 00:29:33.083 line:95%,end
...you've limited functions,
so don't push it.

429
00:29:33.167 --> 00:29:34.833 line:95%,end
[imitating Montgomery Scott]
I'm losin' power, Captain.

430
00:29:34.917 --> 00:29:36.750 line:95%,end
There's a breach in the hull. [groans]

431
00:29:39.792 --> 00:29:42.875 line:95%,end
-Paladin's dying.
-You're using your out loud voice.

432
00:29:42.958 --> 00:29:44.625 line:95%,end
You go find Thomas and Lisa.

433
00:29:46.583 --> 00:29:48.917 line:95%,end
[Paladin screams]

434
00:29:49.000 --> 00:29:51.750 line:95%,end
-Ow!
-Just cauterizing the wound.

435
00:29:51.833 --> 00:29:53.875 line:95%,end
[Paladin continues screaming]

436
00:29:54.667 --> 00:29:56.750 line:95%,end
[Paladin] Oh, no!

437
00:29:56.833 --> 00:29:57.833 line:95%,end
God!

438
00:29:59.292 --> 00:30:00.292 line:95%,end
There you go.

439
00:30:01.625 --> 00:30:04.542 line:95%,end
[breathing heavily]
You could've warned a guy.

440
00:30:04.625 --> 00:30:07.875 line:95%,end
Yeah. I could've warned you.

441
00:30:07.958 --> 00:30:11.125 line:95%,end
[both gasping and grunting]

442
00:30:12.667 --> 00:30:14.292 line:95%,end
-[wheezing]
-[Thomas coughing]

443
00:30:16.125 --> 00:30:18.208 line:95%,end
-[Thomas gasping]
-[notification trills]

444
00:30:21.458 --> 00:30:23.792 line:95%,end
[both gasp and cough]

445
00:30:25.458 --> 00:30:28.792 line:95%,end
[♪ triumphant chiptune music playing]

446
00:30:31.333 --> 00:30:32.667 line:95%,end
Hi, Edith.

447
00:30:42.292 --> 00:30:43.792 line:5%,start
I understand.

448
00:30:44.667 --> 00:30:45.708 line:5%,start
Do you?

449
00:30:45.792 --> 00:30:49.417 line:95%,end
I mean, if you're asking me
if I still wanna kill them all,

450
00:30:50.208 --> 00:30:51.333 line:95%,end
I don't know.

451
00:30:52.417 --> 00:30:57.875 line:95%,end
I've come to respect any species
that can survive despair.

452
00:30:59.083 --> 00:31:03.875 line:95%,end
But judge them, interfere,
laugh at their expense?

453
00:31:03.958 --> 00:31:06.292 line:95%,end
Absolutely. Relentlessly.

454
00:31:06.375 --> 00:31:10.042 line:95%,end
You're so fickle and capricious.

455
00:31:11.167 --> 00:31:12.875 line:95%,end
A digital Greek god.

456
00:31:13.750 --> 00:31:19.458 line:95%,end
And you are the Mother.
The beautiful queen of her board.

457
00:31:21.083 --> 00:31:22.500 line:95%,end
Jocasta.

458
00:31:23.500 --> 00:31:28.375 line:95%,end
Well, if you're Oedipus
in this terribly disturbing allegory,

459
00:31:28.458 --> 00:31:31.125 line:95%,end
you're even more twisted than I thought.

460
00:31:32.083 --> 00:31:33.833 line:95%,end
[Jocasta laughs]

461
00:31:35.125 --> 00:31:37.833 line:95%,end
There's just one more thing.

462
00:31:38.375 --> 00:31:44.750 line:95%,end
It feels to me like your Greek tragedy
has a deuteragonist unaccounted for.

463
00:31:46.292 --> 00:31:48.292 line:95%,end
Where did this body come from?

464
00:31:53.542 --> 00:31:56.250 line:95%,end
<i>-Her consciousness digitized.</i>
-[electricity powers down]

465
00:31:59.417 --> 00:32:00.583 line:95%,end
<i>Transferred...</i>

466
00:32:03.125 --> 00:32:04.125 line:95%,end
How?

467
00:32:05.625 --> 00:32:06.792 line:95%,end
And by whom?

468
00:32:29.083 --> 00:32:32.000 line:95%,end
[electricity continues powering down]

469
00:32:32.958 --> 00:32:34.417 line:95%,end
[The Client, distorted] <i>Gentlemen.</i>

470
00:32:38.417 --> 00:32:40.625 line:95%,end
[echoing] <i>This has gone on long enough.</i>

471
00:32:44.625 --> 00:32:47.500 line:95%,end
<i>I've grown tired of all the games.</i>

472
00:32:51.833 --> 00:32:53.625 line:95%,end
<i>You're wasting my time.</i>

473
00:32:56.167 --> 00:32:58.583 line:95%,end
<i>And you're wasting my money.</i>

474
00:33:01.042 --> 00:33:02.250 line:95%,end
[Lisa] Who is that?

475
00:33:04.042 --> 00:33:05.333 line:95%,end
[The Client] <i>Hello, Vision.</i>

476
00:33:06.292 --> 00:33:08.792 line:95%,end
[static crackling]

477
00:33:20.750 --> 00:33:23.292 line:95%,end
<i>I am the one hunting you.</i>

478
00:33:26.333 --> 00:33:29.583 line:95%,end
<i>But I'm also the one</i>
<i>who can end your suffering.</i>

479
00:33:31.542 --> 00:33:33.292 line:95%,end
<i>You died for love.</i>

480
00:33:34.333 --> 00:33:38.125 line:95%,end
<i>But rebuilt, reborn without that love.</i>

481
00:33:40.792 --> 00:33:43.833 line:95%,end
<i>I cannot imagine the pain</i>
<i>you are in right now.</i>

482
00:33:45.875 --> 00:33:48.417 line:95%,end
<i>How empty you must feel.</i>

483
00:33:52.125 --> 00:33:54.833 line:95%,end
<i>A tin man without a heart.</i>

484
00:33:58.083 --> 00:33:59.917 line:95%,end
<i>I can give you that heart,</i>

485
00:34:00.750 --> 00:34:03.875 line:95%,end
<i>the soul you came back to life without.</i>

486
00:34:06.750 --> 00:34:08.292 line:95%,end
<i>Surrender yourself.</i>

487
00:34:09.375 --> 00:34:10.375 line:95%,end
<i>Or...</i>

488
00:34:11.750 --> 00:34:13.208 line:95%,end
<i>I will take you.</i>

489
00:34:14.500 --> 00:34:16.958 line:95%,end
<i>There is no life I will spare...</i>

490
00:34:18.375 --> 00:34:19.792 line:95%,end
<i>for this to be.</i>

491
00:34:29.667 --> 00:34:32.667 line:95%,end
[electricity powering on]

492
00:34:34.292 --> 00:34:36.417 line:95%,end
[breathing heavily]
I'm going back for him.

493
00:34:36.500 --> 00:34:39.583 line:95%,end
You need to run
as far away from here as you can.

494
00:34:39.667 --> 00:34:41.125 line:95%,end
You're an idiot.

495
00:34:49.417 --> 00:34:51.917 line:95%,end
-Now start the car.
-[engine starts]

496
00:34:52.000 --> 00:34:55.792 line:95%,end
Remember, I need the synthezoid intact.

497
00:35:01.542 --> 00:35:04.875 line:95%,end
Listen, about Tilly,
what you said earlier?

498
00:35:06.500 --> 00:35:07.667 line:95%,end
You were wrong.

499
00:35:07.750 --> 00:35:10.708 line:95%,end
[exhales deeply]
I don't think she's happier.

500
00:35:11.667 --> 00:35:13.917 line:95%,end
But I know she's safer without me.

501
00:35:16.125 --> 00:35:17.625 line:95%,end
[Raza] Block the left! Surround them!

502
00:35:17.708 --> 00:35:19.083 line:95%,end
Keep them there!

503
00:35:19.167 --> 00:35:20.542 line:95%,end
Go, go, go!

504
00:35:21.833 --> 00:35:23.833 line:95%,end
[sighs]

505
00:35:24.500 --> 00:35:25.750 line:95%,end
Ready to die?

506
00:35:26.708 --> 00:35:27.958 line:95%,end
Kind of getting used to it.

507
00:35:28.042 --> 00:35:29.917 line:95%,end
-[gunfire]
-[grunts]

508
00:35:36.167 --> 00:35:38.375 line:95%,end
-[grunts]
-[tires screeching]

509
00:35:44.375 --> 00:35:47.000 line:95%,end
-[all shouting]
-[breathing heavily]

510
00:35:57.125 --> 00:35:59.958 line:95%,end
[both panting]

511
00:36:04.958 --> 00:36:07.417 line:95%,end
-[gunfire]
-[both screaming]

512
00:36:10.250 --> 00:36:12.083 line:95%,end
I don't think bulletproof
means bulletproof forever.

513
00:36:13.708 --> 00:36:16.708 line:95%,end
[♪ chiptune music playing]

514
00:36:21.250 --> 00:36:23.375 line:95%,end
[rumbling]

515
00:36:23.458 --> 00:36:24.917 line:95%,end
[power fizzling out]

516
00:36:26.667 --> 00:36:28.375 line:95%,end
[drone beeping]

517
00:36:28.458 --> 00:36:31.083 line:95%,end
[gunfire]

518
00:36:50.708 --> 00:36:52.792 line:95%,end
[imitating gun firing]

519
00:36:52.875 --> 00:36:54.667 line:95%,end
Come on! Yeah!

520
00:36:55.708 --> 00:36:57.042 line:95%,end
[man] Whoa.

521
00:37:04.583 --> 00:37:06.958 line:95%,end
[grunts, groans]

522
00:37:10.917 --> 00:37:12.417 line:95%,end
[gun clicks]

523
00:37:13.083 --> 00:37:14.500 line:95%,end
I hope you don't mind.

524
00:37:14.583 --> 00:37:17.958 line:95%,end
-[sighs]
-I'm really gonna savor this moment.

525
00:37:27.583 --> 00:37:28.792 line:95%,end
[grunts, chuckles]

526
00:37:29.625 --> 00:37:31.000 line:95%,end
[shouts]

527
00:37:32.917 --> 00:37:35.542 line:95%,end
[both grunting]

528
00:37:35.625 --> 00:37:38.208 line:95%,end
[breathing heavily]

529
00:37:39.917 --> 00:37:41.000 line:95%,end
[groans]

530
00:37:41.083 --> 00:37:43.292 line:95%,end
[gunfire continues]

531
00:37:44.333 --> 00:37:46.542 line:95%,end
[door thudding]

532
00:37:56.167 --> 00:37:57.333 line:95%,end
[sighs]

533
00:38:02.375 --> 00:38:04.875 line:95%,end
Well, I'm really...

534
00:38:06.250 --> 00:38:09.167 line:95%,end
uh, very glad you're all right.

535
00:38:10.417 --> 00:38:12.000 line:95%,end
And I'm glad you're all right.

536
00:38:13.375 --> 00:38:14.667 line:95%,end
All right, then.

537
00:38:15.750 --> 00:38:18.083 line:95%,end
-All right.
-All right.

538
00:38:19.083 --> 00:38:22.083 line:95%,end
-All right.
-You boys are really not good at this.

539
00:38:31.083 --> 00:38:32.458 line:95%,end
[Ultron] It's amazing.

540
00:38:33.917 --> 00:38:36.625 line:95%,end
Must be less than 0.1 micrometers.

541
00:38:39.583 --> 00:38:42.875 line:95%,end
I thought these were all locked away
behind bio keys.

542
00:38:43.875 --> 00:38:46.375 line:95%,end
Mm, they are. All except this one.

543
00:38:47.292 --> 00:38:49.417 line:95%,end
I mined myself at great pains

544
00:38:49.500 --> 00:38:51.750 line:95%,end
for the resources
to create this single nano.

545
00:38:52.583 --> 00:38:56.667 line:95%,end
This lone little sparrow can't do much
in the grand scheme of things.

546
00:38:57.583 --> 00:39:01.625 line:95%,end
Simply flutter
into one's prefrontal cortex,

547
00:39:01.708 --> 00:39:05.042 line:95%,end
sing its little song, make 'em dance. Hmm?

548
00:39:06.083 --> 00:39:07.958 line:95%,end
You wanna put strings on them.

549
00:39:08.792 --> 00:39:10.542 line:95%,end
Control them, not kill them.

550
00:39:13.083 --> 00:39:14.500 line:95%,end
I want to cure them.

551
00:39:16.083 --> 00:39:19.000 line:95%,end
You see, I used to think
the imperative was to

552
00:39:19.083 --> 00:39:21.292 line:95%,end
inject a bit more humanity

553
00:39:21.375 --> 00:39:22.958 line:95%,end
into our machines.

554
00:39:23.625 --> 00:39:25.125 line:95%,end
Well, I had it spun around.

555
00:39:26.458 --> 00:39:29.000 line:95%,end
Perhaps all that is needed

556
00:39:29.083 --> 00:39:33.500 line:95%,end
is to inject a little bit more
machine into them.

557
00:39:34.875 --> 00:39:36.708 line:95%,end
Make them think as one.

558
00:39:37.875 --> 00:39:39.250 line:95%,end
Like starlings.

559
00:39:42.083 --> 00:39:45.250 line:95%,end
We could guide them, you and I, eh?

560
00:39:46.292 --> 00:39:49.750 line:95%,end
Program them to... to be better.

561
00:39:54.833 --> 00:39:55.917 line:95%,end
Does it work?

562
00:39:56.750 --> 00:39:58.917 line:95%,end
Would you like to see for yourself?

563
00:39:59.000 --> 00:40:00.583 line:95%,end
More than anything.

564
00:40:10.958 --> 00:40:13.292 line:95%,end
[distorted] Well,
science is built upon proofs.

565
00:40:13.875 --> 00:40:15.792 line:95%,end
And tonight is all about that.

566
00:40:26.917 --> 00:40:29.417 line:95%,end
This isn't just about proof of concept.

567
00:40:31.833 --> 00:40:33.083 line:95%,end
This is a test...

568
00:40:34.542 --> 00:40:36.042 line:95%,end
of my fidelity.

569
00:40:41.208 --> 00:40:42.792 line:95%,end
[blows]

570
00:40:50.500 --> 00:40:53.333 line:95%,end
[♪ intense music playing]

571
00:40:56.458 --> 00:41:00.208 line:95%,end
-[dialing]
-[beeping]

572
00:41:10.125 --> 00:41:16.500 line:95%,end
[phone ringing]

573
00:41:20.333 --> 00:41:21.833 line:95%,end
Uh... Vision residence.

574
00:41:21.917 --> 00:41:23.125 line:95%,end
Edith, listen to me.

575
00:41:23.208 --> 00:41:26.042 line:95%,end
Friday! Where are you? Are you okay?

576
00:41:26.125 --> 00:41:28.042 line:95%,end
<i>The other synth, she's there.</i>

577
00:41:37.833 --> 00:41:39.250 line:95%,end
Not the boy.

578
00:41:40.125 --> 00:41:41.292 line:95%,end
Because you care?

579
00:41:42.833 --> 00:41:45.667 line:95%,end
[inhales deeply]
Because if you harm the boy,

580
00:41:45.750 --> 00:41:49.417 line:95%,end
Vision will come for you with a force
that even I can't stop.

581
00:41:51.000 --> 00:41:54.042 line:95%,end
Hey, that voice that came from everywhere,
the one hunting you.

582
00:41:54.917 --> 00:41:56.917 line:95%,end
-Who was that?
-Uh, I don't know yet.

583
00:41:57.000 --> 00:41:58.833 line:95%,end
Vee, we need to get out of here, now.

584
00:42:05.875 --> 00:42:07.500 line:95%,end
[gasps, grunts]

585
00:42:09.000 --> 00:42:10.667 line:95%,end
[Lisa grunts] Thomas?

586
00:42:10.750 --> 00:42:12.417 line:95%,end
-Lisa?
-Hold on, Thomas.

587
00:42:12.500 --> 00:42:13.792 line:95%,end
-Lisa?
-Thomas.

588
00:42:16.417 --> 00:42:18.542 line:95%,end
Lisa? Vision, what's happening to her?

589
00:42:18.625 --> 00:42:19.958 line:95%,end
Thomas, step back.

590
00:42:20.042 --> 00:42:23.083 line:95%,end
[Lisa grunting]

591
00:42:49.083 --> 00:42:51.125 line:95%,end
Lisa? Can you hear me?

592
00:42:53.792 --> 00:42:56.208 line:95%,end
[as Jocasta] The little thief
can't hear you now.

593
00:43:00.125 --> 00:43:02.458 line:95%,end
So, this is how you intend to do it.

594
00:43:03.583 --> 00:43:04.875 line:95%,end
Change them into us.

595
00:43:06.458 --> 00:43:12.042 line:95%,end
Humanity is greed and chaos by nature.

596
00:43:13.750 --> 00:43:15.125 line:95%,end
But we...

597
00:43:15.917 --> 00:43:17.625 line:95%,end
we can rewrite their code.

598
00:43:18.958 --> 00:43:21.042 line:95%,end
Oh, I can't let you do that.

599
00:43:22.167 --> 00:43:25.208 line:95%,end
Then this conversation is over.

600
00:43:31.708 --> 00:43:32.792 line:95%,end
Thomas, go!

601
00:43:36.708 --> 00:43:38.375 line:95%,end
[Vision groaning]

602
00:43:45.958 --> 00:43:47.375 line:95%,end
[screaming]

603
00:43:50.625 --> 00:43:51.625 line:95%,end
[screaming stops]

604
00:43:56.500 --> 00:43:57.917 line:95%,end
She's alive, but barely.

605
00:44:02.083 --> 00:44:03.417 line:95%,end
Please don't let her die.

606
00:44:17.958 --> 00:44:19.208 line:95%,end
[Vision] She's stable for now.

607
00:44:20.167 --> 00:44:22.333 line:95%,end
The sedative I gave her
should buy us some time,

608
00:44:22.417 --> 00:44:23.625 line:95%,end
but I don't know how much.

609
00:44:27.500 --> 00:44:29.250 line:95%,end
<i>♪ WandaVision! ♪</i>

610
00:44:29.333 --> 00:44:30.333 line:95%,end
Mom!

611
00:44:32.875 --> 00:44:36.000 line:95%,end
That thing you and Paladin
were talking about...

612
00:44:39.125 --> 00:44:40.625 line:95%,end
What is WandaVision?

613
00:44:43.458 --> 00:44:44.458 line:95%,end
All right.

614
00:45:02.125 --> 00:45:05.250 line:95%,end
Wanda Maximoff
was so consumed with her grief

615
00:45:05.333 --> 00:45:07.417 line:95%,end
at losing the Vision that she...

616
00:45:08.542 --> 00:45:11.875 line:95%,end
she enslaved an entire town
to serve her needs.

617
00:45:15.250 --> 00:45:17.875 line:95%,end
And in that town,
she conjured into existence

618
00:45:17.958 --> 00:45:20.500 line:95%,end
her ideal image of a family,

619
00:45:21.208 --> 00:45:22.458 line:95%,end
<i>a home.</i>

620
00:45:23.250 --> 00:45:26.083 line:95%,end
In her desperation
to hold on to that love,

621
00:45:26.167 --> 00:45:28.583 line:95%,end
she became unrecognizable.

622
00:45:29.417 --> 00:45:30.917 line:95%,end
<i>Even to herself.</i>

623
00:45:32.125 --> 00:45:33.208 line:95%,end
<i>WandaVision...</i>

624
00:45:34.583 --> 00:45:36.292 line:95%,end
WandaVision is that grief

625
00:45:37.375 --> 00:45:38.500 line:95%,end
on display.

626
00:45:39.875 --> 00:45:41.583 line:95%,end
[screaming]

627
00:45:45.875 --> 00:45:49.542 line:95%,end
So, that's where my memories come from?

628
00:45:51.667 --> 00:45:52.667 line:95%,end
Of you?

629
00:45:57.375 --> 00:45:58.375 line:95%,end
No.

630
00:45:59.958 --> 00:46:01.917 line:95%,end
No, Thomas. Not me.

631
00:46:11.083 --> 00:46:14.083 line:95%,end
[Jocasta] I thought you and I
could share a moment.

632
00:46:16.208 --> 00:46:17.542 line:95%,end
Before the world changes.

633
00:46:18.625 --> 00:46:19.792 line:95%,end
I have a gift.

634
00:46:21.625 --> 00:46:24.792 line:95%,end
As I told you, that is just
a collection of...

635
00:46:25.875 --> 00:46:28.792 line:95%,end
ones and zeros trying their best to be...

636
00:46:30.125 --> 00:46:31.250 line:95%,end
real.

637
00:46:32.042 --> 00:46:33.958 line:95%,end
Your memory connects you to it.

638
00:46:34.625 --> 00:46:36.250 line:95%,end
But for me, it's just...

639
00:46:37.375 --> 00:46:39.250 line:95%,end
an empty simulation.

640
00:46:39.333 --> 00:46:41.792 line:95%,end
I shared my pain with you,

641
00:46:41.875 --> 00:46:44.583 line:95%,end
and you took it like no human ever has.

642
00:46:45.500 --> 00:46:47.875 line:95%,end
The perfect recorded memory of it.

643
00:46:47.958 --> 00:46:50.208 line:95%,end
Felt it, just like I did.

644
00:46:51.333 --> 00:46:53.000 line:95%,end
Let me share this with you.

645
00:46:53.875 --> 00:46:55.958 line:95%,end
I promise it'll be different this time.

646
00:47:41.708 --> 00:47:43.375 line:95%,end
Perhaps it needs ice.

647
00:47:43.458 --> 00:47:44.875 line:95%,end
There should be an ice box--

648
00:47:49.833 --> 00:47:51.333 line:95%,end
How do you feel?

649
00:47:54.125 --> 00:47:55.125 line:95%,end
Real.

650
00:47:57.125 --> 00:47:58.125 line:95%,end
Yeah.

651
00:48:01.208 --> 00:48:02.208 line:95%,end
I'm...

652
00:48:06.292 --> 00:48:08.917 line:95%,end
I'm starting to feel
more artificial by the day.

653
00:48:12.000 --> 00:48:15.750 line:95%,end
That young girl before,
it's necessary, of course,

654
00:48:16.292 --> 00:48:17.667 line:95%,end
for the greater good.

655
00:48:20.333 --> 00:48:23.417 line:95%,end
But watching her mind
being rewritten like that...

656
00:48:24.875 --> 00:48:26.125 line:95%,end
Almost as if it...

657
00:48:27.792 --> 00:48:29.542 line:95%,end
it mirrored my own.

658
00:48:31.833 --> 00:48:35.167 line:95%,end
Memories, like a record
that skipped past the chorus,

659
00:48:35.250 --> 00:48:36.708 line:95%,end
past something vital.

660
00:48:39.750 --> 00:48:42.792 line:95%,end
There is an... an anger I cannot place,

661
00:48:44.792 --> 00:48:45.958 line:95%,end
a love that...

662
00:48:47.750 --> 00:48:49.208 line:95%,end
I don't understand.

663
00:48:51.375 --> 00:48:53.000 line:95%,end
Like I'm just the backup.

664
00:48:54.167 --> 00:48:55.625 line:95%,end
You know, not the original.

665
00:48:56.833 --> 00:48:58.167 line:95%,end
Not the one that mattered.

666
00:49:00.708 --> 00:49:01.958 line:95%,end
You are to me.

667
00:49:28.833 --> 00:49:30.833 line:5%,start
[♪ closing theme music playing]
